  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "id": "s0001",
          "zh": "康熙壬子年恒星黃道經緯度表一 揆日所以正時，候星所以紀日。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "Kangxi renzi year—fixed-star ecliptic longitude and latitude table, scroll one. Gauging the sun is how one corrects time; observing stars is how one records days.",
              "idiomatic": "Fixed-star ecliptic coordinates, Kangxi renzi (1672), table 1: the sun sets the clock; the stars mark the calendar.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2.5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0002",
          "zh": "日行黃道，故推測恒星，必求黃道經緯度分。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "The sun travels the ecliptic, so in computing fixed stars one must obtain ecliptic longitude and latitude in degrees and minutes.",
              "idiomatic": "Because the sun moves along the ecliptic, fixed-star work requires ecliptic longitude and latitude to the minute.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2.5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0003",
          "zh": "且恒星循黃道東行，上考下求，每年祗加減經度五十一秒。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "Moreover fixed stars drift east along the ecliptic; comparing upward or seeking downward, each year one need only add or subtract fifty-one seconds of longitude.",
              "idiomatic": "Stars also creep eastward on the ecliptic; for any epoch, adjust longitude by only fifty-one seconds per year.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2.5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0004",
          "zh": "今依康熙壬子舊測恒星黃道經緯度分，及南北之向，大小之等，為二卷。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "Now according to the Kangxi renzi former survey of fixed stars' ecliptic longitude and latitude in degrees and minutes, and their north-south bearing and magnitude rank, are made two scrolls.",
              "idiomatic": "This edition follows the Kangxi renzi star survey—longitude, latitude, hemisphere, and magnitude—in two scrolls.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2.5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0005",
          "zh": "先列降婁戌宮至鶉尾巳宮，凡一百八十度之名星及附近星，如左：",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "First are listed from Lowering Harvest Xu palace to Quail Tail Si palace, all named stars within one hundred eighty degrees and nearby stars, as at left:",
              "idiomatic": "Scroll one lists every named star—and neighbors—across one hundred eighty degrees from Lowering Harvest (Xu) to Quail Tail (Si), as follows.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2.5"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "literal": "",
          "idiomatic": "",
          "translator": ""
        }
      ]
    },
